gitree (0.3.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * While the diff fills the window, a close button shows at its top
    right. A click on it brings back the refs and the list, and the diff
    stays open.
  * A double click or Enter on a commit that changes one file fills the
    window with the diff at once.
  * A click that closes a file, or a click on Collapse all, does not fill
    the window. In 0.2.0 it did.
  * A file in the diff closes at once when you click it. Before, its text
    stayed on the screen for a quarter of a second.

 -- alexandros filotheou <alexandros.filotheou@gmail.com>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:35:16 +0200

gitree (0.2.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * The refs on the left follow the order of the graph. A ref whose
    commit is higher in the history comes first, and a group takes the
    place of its highest ref.
  * The details pane opens below the refs and the list, and it is as wide
    as the window.
  * A click on a file, or on Expand all, fills the window with the diff.
    Escape or the back arrow brings back the refs and the list.
  * Escape closes the details also when no widget has the focus, for
    example after the divider is dragged to the top.

 -- alexandros filotheou <alexandros.filotheou@gmail.com>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:12:13 +0200

gitree (0.1.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. gitree shows the history of the branches, remote
    branches and tags that you tick, drawn the way gitg draws it. Names
    with slashes fold into groups, a double click on a commit shows its
    details and its diff, and a path keeps only the commits that change a
    file or a folder. The command is gitree, and git tree runs it too.

 -- alexandros filotheou <alexandros.filotheou@gmail.com>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:37:45 +0200
